      "side": 1,
      "message": "`pkvm_reset_vcpu()` doesn\u0027t race with itself. The commit message isn\u0027t clear. I\u0027ve updated it.\n\nThe race is between the *source* vCPU (performing the failure rollback) and the *target* vCPU (executing `pkvm_reset_vcpu()`). This happens if an untrusted host maliciously schedules the target vCPU while concurrently returning a failure to the source vCPU.\n\nRegarding the PSCI semantics for pvmfw: I think they are the same. In both cases, the *primary* vCPU is initialized directly to `ON_PENDING` during VM creation (bypassing guest `CPU_ON`), while *secondary* vCPUs start `OFF` and use the exact same `CPU_ON` path.\n\nDoes that help?",
